# examples/ui/04_settings, played: every kind of control from the keyboard,
# the gamepad and the mouse, a name typed and corrected, applied -- and said
# so at the bottom of the screen -- and then reverted; a value at its limit,
# a disabled box, a list closed without a choice.
#
# The focus starts on Fullscreen, asked for by name, so the ring shows from
# the first frame. A change that animates (a box filling, a colour) takes
# 0.12 s, so a shot waits ten frames. See tests/e2e/script.h.

# --- the happy path: the keyboard and the gamepad ---------------------------

# Enter ticks Fullscreen, and Revert and Apply wake up.
1 tap KEY_ENTER

# Down to VSync, and down again to Master volume: the disabled Subtitles is
# no stop on the way. Right does nothing there -- it is at 100% already.
3 tap KEY_DOWN
5 tap KEY_DOWN
7 tap KEY_RIGHT

# Music, down two steps of 5%: 80% to 70%.
9 tap KEY_DOWN
11 tap KEY_LEFT
13 tap KEY_LEFT

# The gamepad: down past Sensitivity to Quality in the other column, A to
# open its list, down to High.
15 tap GAMEPAD_BUTTON_LEFT_FACE_DOWN
17 tap GAMEPAD_BUTTON_LEFT_FACE_DOWN
19 tap GAMEPAD_BUTTON_RIGHT_FACE_DOWN
21 tap GAMEPAD_BUTTON_LEFT_FACE_DOWN
30 shot quality_list_open

# A picks it.
31 tap GAMEPAD_BUTTON_RIGHT_FACE_DOWN

# Language: opened, walked to Espanol, and closed with Escape -- English
# stays.
33 tap KEY_DOWN
35 tap KEY_ENTER
37 tap KEY_DOWN
39 tap KEY_ESCAPE

# The name field takes the keyboard when the focus arrives on it: " Onf"
# goes on the end, Backspace takes the typo off, and "e" finishes it -- Player
# One. Its caret blinks twice a second on the game's clock: shown for the
# first half of each second, hidden for the second.
41 tap KEY_DOWN
43 type " Onf"
45 tap KEY_BACKSPACE
47 type "e"
52 shot name_caret_shown
82 shot name_caret_hidden

# Down past it to Revert, to Apply, and Enter: kept, nothing is unsaved, and
# "Saved" at the bottom says so for three seconds.
83 tap KEY_DOWN
85 tap KEY_DOWN
87 tap KEY_ENTER
98 shot applied

# --- the mouse, and what does not move --------------------------------------

# VSync off with a click; a click on the disabled Subtitles does nothing; a
# click on Sensitivity's rail puts it there, in steps of 5%.
99 click 63 172
101 click 63 217
103 click 300 355
114 shot clicked

# Revert: back to what Apply kept.
115 click 466 300
126 shot reverted
126 end
